# OpenAI Models

## Available models and default preferences

When using OpenAI API, the following models are available:

### Frontier Models (recommended for most tasks)

| Model ID | Name | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `gpt-5.1` | GPT-5.1 | The best model for coding and agentic tasks with configurable reasoning effort |
| `gpt-5-mini` | GPT-5 mini | A faster, cost-efficient version of GPT-5 for well-defined tasks |
| `gpt-5-nano` | GPT-5 nano | Fastest, most cost-efficient version of GPT-5 |
| `gpt-5-pro` | GPT-5 pro | Version of GPT-5 that produces smarter and more precise responses |
| `gpt-5` | GPT-5 | Previous intelligent reasoning model for coding and agentic tasks |
| `gpt-4.1` | GPT-4.1 | Smartest non-reasoning model |

### Default Model Selection

**Always use these defaults unless specified otherwise:**

- **Default for most tasks:** `gpt-5-mini` - Good balance of speed, cost, and capability
- **Default for simple/fast tasks:** `gpt-5-nano` - When speed and cost matter most
- **For complex reasoning:** `gpt-5.1` or `gpt-5-pro` - Only when explicitly needed

### Code Example

```python
# Default model constant
MODEL_NAME = "gpt-5-mini"  # Use this as default

# For simpler extraction tasks
FAST_MODEL = "gpt-5-nano"

# For complex reasoning (use sparingly)
REASONING_MODEL = "gpt-5.1"
```







